 "source": "# Block scalars. Interior is content, not layout: prettier does not reflow\n# a `>` line that overruns the width, and a relative extra indent is data.\n\n# Literal: newlines kept. Already at prettier's 2-space block indent so a\n# reindent does not change the block_scalar leaf text gate 3 compares.\nscript : | # clip is the default\n  echo hello\n  echo world\n\n# Folded: newlines become spaces. Prettier leaves the source line-breaks.\ndesc:  >\n  This is a fairly long folded description that would overflow forty columns if reflowed onto one line of the document.\n\n# Chomping indicators. strip / keep / clip are three different spellings.\nstrip : |-\n  no final newline\n\nkeep:  |+\n  keep blanks\n\n\nclip : |\n  clip default\n\n# Indent indicator: the `2` is part of the token. Content starts two\n# columns past the parent, so four leading spaces are two of content.\nnote:  |2\n    four spaces of content, two of them data\n\n# Relative extra indent inside a literal is content and must survive.\nindented : |\n  echo hello\n    nested\n  echo world\n\nfolded_strip:  >-\n  Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious words go here to see if prettier wraps the folded content itself when the source line is long enough to overflow.\n",
